Seriously, this is probably (and easily) of one my favorite games ever.
+ The gameplay is very fluid and tight;
+ The story, although not easy to fully understand from the game (you need to join a lot of pieces of information on your own, and sometimes you'll even miss many of these while exploring the areas), is very detailed and captivating, in my opinion;
+ There are some pretty hard things to beat in the game, and beating bosses is extremely satisfying;
+ I really like how the game handles the exploration aspect. You buy a crude map for each area and complete it yourself in your adventures. This means you have literally no idea what you'll find when you start exploring a place, which I find engaging;
+ The music. I literally cannot say in words how fitting and amazing the songs are, especially for bosses (the last boss' song, for instance, gives me chills every time I decide to fight him - and I already did it a lot of times!);
+ The artwork and the atmosphere are, in my opinion, very, very fitting!
+ There is SO MUCH to do in it. As of now, I have 82.9 hours in total, and I still didn't do everything I can do in it (there are still some upgrades I can find and some other things I still need to do)
- (honestly, I cannot think of anything I disliked in this game)
Overall, I do believe this is a masterpiece, and I cannot recommend it enough! =)

