Great game for anyone into old school shooters like Doom, Duke Nukem 3D, etc. Tons of action, lots of secrets, plenty of easter eggs, held together by solid plot.
It also has cookies.
What I liked the most:
Nice set of guns;
Plenty of environmental (explosive) objects;
Different enemies require different approaches;
Rabbits.
What I did not like:
RPG stuff is kinda bloated - I did not have a chance to use all of my skills I gained. In most cases, game is just about "shoot and slash them all";
Some people claim that graphics were slightly outdated for its release - maybe, I don't care, I'm here for the gameplay ;)
Gameplay is awesome but nothing particularilly revolutionary. And it stays the same way for all game, though you wouldn't complain - it's pretty cool the way it already is ;)
But really, when all you can tell is nothing being revolutionary and vagueness of RPG elements in old school FPS, things are pretty cool. 9/10 in my personal chart.

