TL:DR: No matter how good you think this game is, DO NOT BUY THIIS UNSUPPORTED AND BUG-RIDDEN SOFTWARE
While this game offers compelling action gameplay, character building and 3-player co-op, the bugs will suck your will to play it. I have spent a similar amount of time troubleshooting the game as I have playing it.
I have played this game in local co-op mode (3 players, LAN) and we have had:
- game not running after install;
- multiple re-installs;
- blank screen at Mount Gundabad;
- one player being constantly kicked out of the party at Rivendell;
- at least one player per session being randomly kicked from the hosted match;
- Other small performance, inventory, graphical, sound and quality of life bugs.
Running the game across 3 laptops, 1 Windows 7 and 2 Windows 8.1. No superfluous software running in the background and all video drivers were current and windows updatd to current.
This game would only be suitable for someone who is a single-player masochist who is willing to either run with multiple saves and/or unintended means to get over the bugs. A shame, as it is a good concept poorly executed and now consigned to abandonware.

It's a good game and it has that "Hitman" feeling despite levels being separated into chunks. If you haven't played Hitman before, I'd recommend to start with "Blood Money" and continue to "Absolution" afterwards.
There are a couple of downsides and purely bad application design decissions in "Absolution" which I will mention here. Please note that the game itself leaves a positive experience and that by no means you should judge it by its flaws. I simply had to put them in a review. So:
- Idea of depletable Instinct is debatable at best. It brings some additional gameplay, like searching for a disguise that will allow you to go through a level without spending much Instinct, but it is more flawed than useful;
- Many objects which you can pick up are not clearly visible without using Instinct. I have looked at the statistics page in the game and it showed that I spent about 40% of time in Instinct mode (I always do the first playthrough of a game on Easy, just to get the feel of it). If the developers envisioned that Instinct should be introduced and linked to hiding/pathfinding/rapid execution, that's fine... I guess... most of the time. But there is no reason whatsoever to force players to use it just so we can see where object that we can pick up are.
- The Instinct is NOT a "turn on/turn off" command. It's a "press and hold". That means one of your fingers will have to take one for the team: If you play it for a long time, you WILL feel pain. That's, at least in my book, a no-brainer that could be avoided during the development just by actually looking at how many features are linked with Instinct. You are using it to:
+ find targets and guards;
+ track movement of targets and guards;
+ find routes (for example to see where ladders are);
+ find weapons and ammo;
+ find mission objectives;
+ move past the guards even when you are wearing a disguise;
+ use rapid execution mode;
That's all OK and you could avoid the most of the above when you have played the level already and know where things are, but you'll have to learn the levels somehow and the best way (and the only logical) is to use Instinct. You are bound to use it a lot at least in the first playthrough and that's many hours of one of your fingers stuck on holding one button which WILL cause discomfort.
Apart from the above, it's a good and fun game with great replay value.
Overall, 7/10

To start this review I would say that this isn't Final Fantasy, and do not buy this game even if you have that itch that I had: "OMG Final fantasy is always awesome, this game can't be that bad". Believe me it is!
The game has good graphics and that is the only good thing about it.
The bad things would make and extensive list, so I'm going to make it quick:
-It's an interactive movie, not a video game, for every 20 meters there's a cutscene. And thoose 20 meters are straight forward;
-There are no cities like all the other final fantasy games had, therefore no rest and NO MINIGAMES!!!!!!!
-The combat system is based on auto attacks and magics, it's actually quite stressing to use the manual commands, so you should better forget them;
-This is clearly not a final fantasy game, altough it has a baby chocobo in the hair of a character;
-This could be sold as a Mod for the "Last Remnant" game, because they are quite similar in the main game mechanics;
-The plot and character depth that has always been a strong part of the final fantasy series isn't here, it's has a weak plot and weak characters;

